{{- /* internal/render/templates/envelope.gohtml — the envelope strip
(§7.1): ref, repo, store.enabled, head_check, total, unreadable, laid
out as one full-width flexbox strip (styling is bead .5's; this file
only supplies the structure and class names), never collapsed — it is
what orients a reader before anything else, so it is never behind a
<details>. Dot is htmlEnvelopeView (internal/render/html_view_envelope.go).

head_check.source renders exactly as reported, "none" and "unavailable"
included (§12) — it is never omitted or dressed up as if a check ran.
is_head only appears when HeadCheckHasIsHead is true (source == "repo"),
and diverged only when HeadCheckHasDiverged is true (nil means the check
did not apply; an empty, non-nil Diverged still renders "0 diverged",
distinguishing "checked, found nothing" from "did not check" per §4.3.1
of combined-reviews.md). */ -}}
{{define "envelope"}}
<div id="envelope" class="envelope">
<span class="envelope-ref">collect-reviews: {{.Ref}}</span>
<span class="envelope-repo">repo: {{.RepoName}} ({{if .RepoKnown}}known{{else}}unknown{{end}})</span>
<span class="envelope-store">store: {{if .StoreEnabled}}enabled{{else}}disabled{{end}}</span>
<span class="envelope-head-check">head_check: {{.HeadCheckSource}}{{if .HeadCheckHasIsHead}}, is_head={{.HeadCheckIsHead}}{{end}}{{if .HeadCheckHasDiverged}}, {{.HeadCheckDiverged}} diverged{{end}}</span>
<span class="envelope-total">total: {{.Total}}</span>
<span class="envelope-unreadable">unreadable: {{.Unreadable}}</span>
</div>
{{end}}
